{
  "version": 1,
  "description": "secrets' transition-to-hook-action table (docs/design/secrets.md \u00a711.1 and \u00a711.5), checked against the aweb.hooks catalog. use_transitions maps each dispatch-machine state, plus the approve decision that does not change it, to a post-secret-use-hook action with example events. governance_acts maps secrets' governance acts to post-governance-hook acts and directions. S13's tests read this table. Identifiers and digests are fixtures. Its did:aw derives from the Ed25519 seed of 32 bytes of 0x01. b3_lifecycle exhaustively maps B3 approver audit kinds, including local-only notifications; its payload examples use only the existing catalog. Completion examples cite the original designation or contact-change proof, not a new assertion. b3_payload_refusals are catalog-level invalid variants, not tests of the sink's restricted authority association. job_current_revisions illustrates first creation, a changed-body CURRENT revision and an admitted restore of a stored body; definition_fixture names are restricted-state fixture labels, not hook fields. job_payload_refusals are catalog-level variants, not a production revision-association proof.",
